            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "In addition to simulating the land carbon cycle, FOCI incorporates the Model of Oceanic Pelagic Stoichiometry (MOPS) (Kriest & Oschlies, 2015) to enable the representation of marine biogeochemical processes and the ocean carbon cycle. MOPS resolves biological dynamics such as phytoplankton carbon uptake and remineralisation, calcite formation and dissolution (Chien et al., 2022). In FOCI, both alkalinity and DIC agree well with observations, while still showing a positive bias at the surface and a negative bias below 3000 meters of depth (Chien et al., 2022). Most DIC variations are due to OM build-up and CO2 flux variations, while alkalinity is a prognostic tracer simulated as a combination of biological sources and sinks with: nitrate and phosphate supply as sinks, calcium carbonate production and dissolution as sink and source, respectively, and OM formation and remineralisation as sink and source, respectively (Chien et al., 2022).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "MOPS",
            "source_entity_type": "SourceComponent",
            "relation": "PRODUCES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "DIC",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "In addition to simulating the land carbon cycle, FOCI incorporates the Model of Oceanic Pelagic Stoichiometry (MOPS) (Kriest & Oschlies, 2015) to enable the representation of marine biogeochemical processes and the ocean carbon cycle. MOPS resolves biological dynamics such as phytoplankton carbon uptake and remineralisation, calcite formation and dissolution (Chien et al., 2022). In FOCI, both alkalinity and DIC agree well with observations, while still showing a positive bias at the surface and a negative bias below 3000 meters of depth (Chien et al., 2022). Most DIC variations are due to OM build-up and CO2 flux variations, while alkalinity is a prognostic tracer simulated as a combination of biological sources and sinks with: nitrate and phosphate supply as sinks, calcium carbonate production and dissolution as sink and source, respectively, and OM formation and remineralisation as sink and source, respectively (Chien et al., 2022).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
